 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Good that you asked. A sketch is usually just one character, and it' done in few minutes. A study, on the other hand, can have multiple characters and takes longer to draw. Kind of. It's more than just one drawing, though. It' a body of work that helps you hone your skills. Lovely. Do small sketches first to get the light right? Then start again each time you change a light source. You' be amazed at how much it improves. The basics first. Line drawing, value, and a few simple colors. Once you' happy with that, come back with full color. Enjoyable way to spend an evening. A full bottle of wine helps too.",
